M4.23 backup monitor zsh status-variable diagnosis
Date: 2026-08-28

Error image
-----------
The first local polling loop stopped with `read-only variable: status` before
it could print the remote backup service state.

Cause
-----
The local shell is zsh, where `status` is a reserved read-only parameter. The
poller attempted to assign the remote read-only service summary to that name.

Risk
----
None to the running backup or server state. The separately issued server-side
backup start had already succeeded and continued independently. The failed
command performed no server write and did not stop or restart the service.

Rollback
--------
No server rollback is required. This diagnosis can be reverted with the M4.23
deployment-evidence branch.

Approved continuation
---------------------
Repeat only the read-only service polling with `backup_state` as the local
variable, fail immediately on a server-side failed state and continue only
after an inactive/success/zero-exit result.
